integ5 0082 = patches/exl3r/0068-exl3-decode-the-4-bit-chain-as-dependent-launches.patch (overnight 2026-10-31), renumbered for the integrated stack on 3f94715d.

exl3 decode: the 4-bit read-once chain as dependent launches (rot_in, gate/up, epilogue, down) (exl3r c3, 2026-10-31)

On 0067. The decode chain's kernels launch with programmatic stream serialization (cuda/exl3_experts.zig core: `.pdl`
when both projections take the new kernels; TF_EXL3_PDL=0 turns it off, the same bits), so each one's launch and its
prologue overlap the kernel before it. Hazard rules as pdl5's: before griddepcontrol.wait only immutable loads and the
plan; every read of another grid's output and every scratch write after it; every CTA waits (no exit before a wait).
- tf_exl3_experts_rot_in, tf_exl3_gateup_epilogue: wait, then trigger, at entry (no-ops in ordinary launches).
- tf_exl3_grouped_1_k8r8p / _k8r16p (new; Load SHFL_PDL): before the wait the plan (ucount, uids, members: from the
  router two launches back, finished because rot_in and the epilogue wait before they trigger), the trellis pointer and
  width tables and the first k tile's words (immutable); the rows' A fragments and the partials after it; each early
  exit waits first. sc.z: down writes its partials only after its wait, i.e. after the epilogue has read the gate/up's.
- tf_exl3_down_combine (after the side stream's join event), tf_exl3_group and the prompt kernels: unchanged.
pdl5's SASS gate: rot_in and the epilogue 0 pre-wait loads; the grouped p kernels 14 (the audited plan, table and
first-tile loads), no stores or exits before a wait, the trigger after it.
Measured [M, exl3r bench_pdl, GPU1, 400 W, cold 4-bit, the four kernels back to back in trains of 8]: the chain against
production's rot_in + k8r8/nt4 + epilogue + k8r8/nt4: -6.9 / -8.2 / -7.0 / -10.7 / -13.7 / -14.5% at 1/2/4/8/16/32
rows (0067 alone: -1.2 / -5.5 / -2.8 / -11.1 / -14.8 / -14.3%). Exactness: the dependent chain equals the plain one and
production's in 108 of 108 cells (5 dependent runs a case, rows 1-32).

